\subsection{Source-staged startup-to-Live capture qualification}
\label{sec:p5-staged-capture}

The startup gravity certificate and the full-heading Live certificate have
different attitude quotients and must not be identified by reusing one scalar
angle.  In particular, the normal and timeout quantities obtained from the
startup gravity gate bound the error of the down direction only.  They are tilt
bounds, not bounds on the complete element of $\SO(3)$.  A full-heading source
node is formed only when the implementation has acquired a horizontal magnetic
gauge.  If
\begin{equation}
 \cos\theta_{\perp,H}\ge c_H\ge0,
 \qquad |\delta\psi_H|\le\bar\psi_H<1,
 \label{eq:p5-tilt-yaw-components}
\end{equation}
then the composed full-attitude error satisfies the conservative source bound
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \cos\theta_H\ge
 c_H\sqrt{1-\bar\psi_H^2}
 -\sqrt{1-c_H^2}\,\bar\psi_H .}
 \label{eq:p5-full-attitude-cosine}
\end{equation}
Hence the corresponding Cayley radius is bounded by
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\vct c_H\|
 \le2\sqrt{\frac{1-\underline c_{R,H}}
                   {1+\underline c_{R,H}}},
 \qquad \underline c_{R,H}>-1.}
 \label{eq:p5-full-attitude-cayley}
\end{equation}
Equation~\eqref{eq:p5-full-attitude-cosine} deliberately weakens
$\cos\bar\psi_H$ to $\sqrt{1-\bar\psi_H^2}$ and
$\sin\bar\psi_H$ to $\bar\psi_H$; it therefore requires no fitted trajectory
angle or optimistic trigonometric evaluation.

The implementation timeout is a distinct source branch.  Its gravity-alignment
guard does not require the north-ready flag.  Consequently a timeout may enter
held-bias Live mode before a magnetic heading gauge exists.  Such an execution
is \emph{not} assigned the full-heading radius of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:p5-full-attitude-cayley}.  Until magnetic lock or regauging, its
attitude state is certified on the gravity quotient $\SO(3)/\SO(2)$, i.e. modulo
rotation about gravity.  The magnetic gauge event is then a separate hybrid
transition into the full-heading source family.  This branch split is necessary
for the quantitative theorem: the free-yaw covariance used by the source at an
ungauged handoff is not evidence for a finite true-heading error.

The covariance at the instant of handoff is also substantially sharper than a
generic normal-Live covariance envelope.  During startup the translational
block is held.  The implemented attitude initialization clears the
attitude--linear cross covariance; enabling the linear block resets the latent
OU covariance and all of its cross blocks and resets the $S$-pseudo timer.
Thus, at held-bias Live entrance,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 P_{\theta S}=P_{\theta a_w}=P_{a_wS}=0,
 \qquad K_{\theta S}=0,}
 \label{eq:p5-golive-cross-zero}
\end{equation}
while the independent constructor component of the $S$ covariance remains
$P_{SS,0}=50^2I$ for the deployed initialization.  The first nonzero
$S\to\theta$ gain is therefore bounded by propagating this particular source
stage, rather than by inserting the translation-dominated global Live
$\lambda_{\max}(P)$ into a cross-gain inequality.

Before the first due $S=0$ correction, physical accelerometer and magnetometer
measurements have no $S$ column.  The constructor $(S,p,v)$ covariance therefore
contains a persistent component invisible to those measurements.  At time $T$
its scalar per-axis contribution is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 D_S(T)=50^2+20^2T^2+\frac14T^4,}
 \label{eq:p5-persistent-S-component}
\end{equation}
for the declared startup covariance seeds.  If $U_S(T)$ is a validated upper
bound on the complete pre-first-pseudo $P_{SS}$, the remaining correlated
component obeys
\begin{equation}
 E_S(T):=U_S(T)-D_S(T)\ge0.
 \label{eq:p5-S-excess}
\end{equation}
For an isotropic physical measurement $R=\sigma^2I$, positivity of the joint
covariance and
$\max_{x\ge0}\sqrt{x}/(x+\sigma^2)=1/(2\sigma)$ give the directional bound
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|L_SK\|_2\le\frac{\sqrt{E_S(T)}}{2\sigma},}
 \label{eq:p5-final-S-physical-gain}
\end{equation}
where $L_S$ maps a correction at its source position to $S$ at the first due
pseudo.  This bounds accepted physical corrections while rejected or not-due
branches contribute zero; no favorable gating pattern is selected.

Accordingly the deterministic pre-first-pseudo state satisfies a source-stage
bound of the form
\begin{align}
 \|S(T)\|
 &\le \bar S_0+T\bar p_0+\frac{T^2}{2}\bar v_0
       +\frac{T^3}{6}\bar a_{w,0}
 \nonumber\\
 &\quad+
 \sum_{k\in\mathcal A_a}\frac{\sqrt{E_S(T)}}{2\sigma_a}\|r_{a,k}\|
 +\sum_{k\in\mathcal A_m}\frac{\sqrt{E_S(T)}}{2\sigma_m}\|r_{m,k}\|,
 \label{eq:p5-first-S-state-prefix}
\end{align}
where the stable-OU inequality
$|\phi_{Sa}(T)|\le T^3/6$ is used for the initial latent-acceleration term.
Equation~\eqref{eq:p5-first-S-state-prefix} is evaluated on the same candidate
outer source node as the finite-angle attitude calculation and is therefore a
prefix lemma, not an independent assumption of capture.

The remaining full-heading outer step uses the exact large-angle sector of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-large-angle-sector}.  In particular, the finite physical
accelerometer/magnetometer correction is credited as group dissipation; it is
not treated as an adverse perturbation that must fit inside the much smaller
translation-limited local P3 gap.  The source-correlated covariance, gain,
pseudo phase, and vector geometry must belong to one reachable tuple.  Once the
large-angle sector closes the outer prefix bootstrap, the staged
Eqs.~\eqref{eq:p5-golive-cross-zero}--\eqref{eq:p5-first-S-state-prefix} provide
the early $S\to\theta$ contribution and the resulting outer H funnel can be
iterated only after it overlaps the already-certified inner P4 level.
